OSKit RS — Restart Server
==========================

Minix 3-style service manager. Starts system servers in
dependency order, waits for each to signal ready before
starting the next. No sleep-based timing — pure handshake.

Boot order:
1. Disk server (no dependencies)
2. TFS server (depends on disk)
3. TTY server (no dependencies, but after disk)
4. PM server (no dependencies)
5. VFS server (depends on TFS)

Each server calls `rs_ready()` after initialization to notify
the RS thread. RS blocks until the notification arrives, then
starts the next server.

    module oskit.servers

    import oskit.kernel.{create_thread, kernel_stack_usp, kernel_stack_ssp}
    import oskit.services.{thread_id, notify_send_to, notify_read_self, rs_set_tid}
    import oskit.ipc.{ipc_recv_notify, port_create}

Stack slot counter. Slot 0 is init (created by kernel_main).
Servers start at slot 1.

    var rs_next_slot = 1

    rs_alloc_slot() -> int
        val s = rs_next_slot
        rs_next_slot += 1
        s

Wait for a server to signal ready. RS creates a dummy port
so it can use ipc_recv_notify to block for notifications.

    var rs_port = -1

    rs_wait_ready()
        if rs_port < 0
            rs_port = port_create()
        // Block until notification arrives (result == -2)
        var buf: [1]byte
        val result = ipc_recv_notify(rs_port, &buf[0], 1)
        // result == -2 means notification received
        notify_read_self()

Init TID, stored before RS starts so RS can notify init
when all servers are up.

    var rs_init_tid = -1

    rs_set_init_tid(tid: int)
        rs_init_tid = tid

Server entry points, set by init before starting RS.
Stored as i64 function pointers to avoid circular imports.

    val RS_MAX_SERVERS = 8
    var rs_entries: [8]i64
    var rs_names: [64]byte
    var rs_name_len: [8]int
    var rs_server_count = 0

Register a server to be started by RS. Called by init before
creating the RS thread.

    rs_add_server(entry: i64, name: *byte, nlen: int)
        if rs_server_count >= RS_MAX_SERVERS
            return
        val idx = rs_server_count
        rs_entries[idx] = entry
        rs_name_len[idx] = nlen
        val base = idx * 8
        var i = 0
        while i < nlen
            if i >= 8
                break
            rs_names[base + i] = name[i]
            i += 1
        rs_server_count += 1

The RS main function. Starts all registered servers in order
with synchronous handshake, then notifies init.

    rs_main()
        rs_set_tid(thread_id())

        var i = 0
        while i < rs_server_count
            val slot = rs_next_slot
            rs_next_slot += 1
            val name = string(&rs_names[i * 8], rs_name_len[i])
            create_thread(rs_entries[i], kernel_stack_usp(slot), kernel_stack_ssp(slot), name)
            rs_wait_ready()
            i += 1

        // All servers ready — return to caller (init).
        // Future: RS stays alive as a separate thread to monitor
        // and restart crashed servers.
